WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.600
Having now gotten their first glimpse of&nbsp;
"Despicable Me 4," fans are left wondering just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:12.360
how time in this animated world works, exactly. It&nbsp;
seems to pass for some and stay frozen for others.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.440
The first trailer for "Despicable Me 4" has now&nbsp;
dropped, giving fans a taste of the Minion madness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.560
to come this summer. While the clip doesn't give&nbsp;
away too much about the plot, it nevertheless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:29.080
promises the same spy-style antics, charming&nbsp;
family dynamics, and zany comedy that audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.640
have come to know and love over the animated&nbsp;
franchise's 14 years of box office domination.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.040
One of the most interesting&nbsp;
developments in "Despicable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.400
Me 4" involves Gru and Lucy's new baby, Gru Jr.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.400
"Something is missing!"&nbsp;

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.200
"This guy!"
"Oh-ho! There's my boy!"

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.080
HIs introduction is certain to be&nbsp;
a new source of adorable mayhem and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.800
heartwarming moments as the infant learns&nbsp;
to bond with Gru. But for longtime fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.760
the baby's inclusion also opened&nbsp;
up a perplexing question about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.560
"Despicable Me" franchise as a whole. One&nbsp;
Redditor was among the many viewers asking,

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.600
"This is the fourth movie and Gru has a baby now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.960
so why are those girls not aging? They look&nbsp;
the exact same as they did in the first movie."

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:15.640
It's unlikely that fans would have such&nbsp;
a problem with the lack of aging of Gru's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:21.480
adopted daughters Margo, Edith, and Agnes,&nbsp;
had Gru not had a bouncing baby boy. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:26.320
now that the family has welcomed its newest&nbsp;
member, things are more confusing than ever.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:27.760
Another Redditor observed,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.744
"Giving gru and Lucy a baby but not&nbsp;
aging up the girls is crazy lmao."

00:01:32.744 --> 00:01:35.920
Over on X, formerly known as&nbsp;
Twitter, a user compared the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.480
odd choice to characters in the&nbsp;
"Dragon Ball" universe, saying,

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:44.960
"4 movies in and the girls haven't aged up&nbsp;
They got the goten and trunks treatment."

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:48.080
The decision to give Gru a baby&nbsp;
while leaving his daughters the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.560
same age has some fans trying to grasp&nbsp;
the logistics of the "Despicable Me"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.480
universe. Describing seeing the trailer as a&nbsp;
"mind-bending moment," another X user asked,

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:04.000
"How's Gru got a kid and those girls haven't&nbsp;
aged a day? What's the timeline of these movies?"

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.240
If the events of the "Despicable Me"&nbsp;
movies actually took place in real time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.080
then the fourth movie would occur&nbsp;
seven years after the last adventure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.320
meaning that the girls should have grown up&nbsp;
quite a bit. However, fans have determined that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.800
the franchise's timeline doesn't match the real&nbsp;
world's. One such fan on X suggested of Gru Jr.,

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:25.800
"The kid's [only] a few months old,&nbsp;
a year tops. Throwing in pregnancy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.699
I'd say we're only 18-24&nbsp;
months after the last film."

00:02:29.699 --> 00:02:34.400
Fans have also theorized that 2013's&nbsp;
"Despicable Me 2" takes place a year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.480
after the 2010 original. If that same logic&nbsp;
is applied to "Despicable Me 3," then it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.520
not too much of a stretch to buy into the series&nbsp;
taking place within a five to 10-year timeframe.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.720
While some fans are struggling to wrap their&nbsp;
heads around the age of Gru's daughters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.000
others don't see such a reason&nbsp;
to sweat over the matter. In a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.640
franchise full of over-the-top villains,&nbsp;
crazy gadgets, and goofy yellow goons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:02.280
it's safe to chalk up such lingering questions to&nbsp;
good ol' cartoon logic. One Redditor compared how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.880
the characters in "Despicable Me" age — or don't&nbsp;
— to another famous animated family, writing,

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:12.320
"Audiences aren't watching these movies to see&nbsp;
the characters grow up with the viewer. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.360
the exact same as 'The Simpsons' where we know&nbsp;
what to expect without any needless changes."

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.720
"Oh, Bart, cartoons don't have&nbsp;
to be 100 percent realistic."

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.240
Nevertheless, it closes the door to a&nbsp;
potential opportunity for the "Despicable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.760
Me" to defy expectations. Another Redditor argued,

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.320
"Given that the first one was genuinely&nbsp;
very emotional and heartfelt and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:36.680
about him becoming a dad, instead&nbsp;
of all this stuff with Lucy and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:41.280
new baby they could've so easily done a&nbsp;
sillier version of a 'Toy Story' style&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.560
'kids growing up and dad has to accept&nbsp;
it' type thing across a few films."

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.040
What makes Gru's daughters seeming to stay the&nbsp;
same age so frustrating is that it hampers their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:55.480
development as characters and their relationship&nbsp;
with Gru. Since the first film saw them turn the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.840
once villainous Gru into a loving father, the&nbsp;
girls haven't had as much presence within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.760
franchise. Aging them up and having Gru deal with&nbsp;
the difficulties that come with parenting preteens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:10.360
could have given the sequel an amount of heart&nbsp;
that would surely surprise kids and parents alike.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:15.200
It's unlikely that such lingering questions&nbsp;
will deter viewers from seeing "Despicable Me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:21.765
4," but it will certainly keep some scratching&nbsp;
their heads until its release on July 3, 2024.

